Package: SampleCausal
Title: Sample Size Planning for Selected Causal Inference Methods
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: person("Victor J.", "Vera-Ponce", email = "victor_jvp@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Calculates sample sizes, normal-approximation power, precision,
    and minimum detectable effects for selected causal-inference planning
    methods. Includes weighting methods, external-control prediction and
    recruitment reestimation from matching summaries. Retains explicit
    assumptions, method restrictions, references and historical replay.
    Provides a local Shiny interface and artificial examples. The corrected
    M06-E1 variance is explicitly identified as a local mathematical amendment.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
